
pow2 is undefined.

  pow2 was changed to ipow2.  This is to prevent any conflicts with those
  libraries that have added pow2 as a math function.  ipow2 stands for
  "integer power of 2".

ipw2sun will not compile.

  It only works on big-endian machines.  Solution: use ipw2ppm instead, and
  use the netpbm package to convert ppm to sun raster if you need that format.
  You'll have to take the entry for ipw2sun out of $IPW/src/bin/Makefile.

transpose test fails with a comment about cmpimg usage.

  Linux's getopt (as distributed with Slackware) is broken.  Install the
  getopt that is in the IPW src/etc/getopt directory.  Make sure it is
  in your path previous to the /usr/bin/getopt program, or just replace that
  program the the IPW supplied getopt.

Floating point exception.

  Certain programs compute Pi by callting atan2(0,-1).  This works fine unless
  you have installed the math inline macros, which call the native i386 fpatan
  function, which doesn't like these arguments.  A couple ways around this.
  One, have the code "pi = atan2(0,-1)" replaced by "pi = PI", using the
  predefined PI macro.  Another is to define __NO_MATH_INLINES on the compile
  line, in the linux config file, or right before the atan2 call.  Presumably
  you want these for other math calls though.

install: getopt: not found

  Whoops, your vendor and/or shell doesn't have getopt!  Change directory to
  $IPW/src/etc/getopt, and make install.  Install should be able to find the
  new getopt now.

ld: $IPW/lib/libipw.a: warning: archive has no table of contents...

  You need to have ranlib defined in $IPW/lib/make/local.

randomize: paste: not found

  paste is a POSIX, XPG, and SVID2 standard, so you ought to have it.  But...
It's available from GNU (ftp to prep.ai.mit.edu:/pub/gnu) in the textutils
package (textutils-1.12.tar.gz currently).
